- ### Evolution
+ ### Evolution

- A diff compares two versions. An *evolution* follows each element through many. A value which is
- in the first version and the last is recognized as the same value, even if it disappeared and
- came back in between:
+ Ein Diff vergleicht zwei Versionen. Eine *Evolution* verfolgt jedes Element durch viele. Ein
+ Wert, der in der ersten und in der letzten Version vorkommt, wird als derselbe Wert erkannt,
+ selbst wenn er zwischendurch verschwunden und wiedergekehrt ist:

= came back in between:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val versions = List(List('d', 'o', 'g'), List('c', 'a', 't'), List('d', 'o', 'g'))
+ val versions = List(List('d', 'o', 'g'), List('c', 'a', 't'), List('d', 'o', 'g'))

- val evolution = evolve(versions)
+ val evolution = evolve(versions)

= val evolution = evolve(versions)
- ```
+ ```

- Each version is addressed by an ordinal, and is reconstructed exactly as it was:
+ Jede Version wird über eine Ordinalzahl angesprochen und genau so rekonstruiert, wie sie war:

= Each version is addressed by an ordinal, and is reconstructed exactly as it was:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= Each version is addressed by an ordinal, and is reconstructed exactly as it was:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= Each version is addressed by an ordinal, and is reconstructed exactly as it was:
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- Out.println(evolution(Ter).inspect)
+ Out.println(evolution(Ter).inspect)

= Out.println(evolution(Ter).inspect)
- ```
+ ```

- This is the structure which a document history, an undo stack or a series of drafts needs.
+ Dies ist die Struktur, die eine Dokumenthistorie, ein Undo-Stapel oder eine Reihe von Entwürfen
+ braucht.

